<p>Use the following procedure to print with a custom paper size.</p>
<p class="Note">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>A paper size mismatch error may occur due to a 
 miscalculation in the paper size.</p></li>
</ul>
<h2>Printing on Custom Size Paper Whose Size Has Not Been Registered Yet</h2>
<ol>
<li><p>Open the printing preferences dialog box after 
 creating a document in an application.</p></li>
<li><p>Click the <span class="Term-Soft">Frequently Used 
 Settings</span> tab or the <span class="Term-Soft">Basic</span> menu on 
 the <span class="Term-Soft">Detailed Settings</span> tab.</p></li>
<li><p>Click <span class="Term-Soft">Custom Paper Size...</span> 
 to open the dialog box.</p></li>
</ol>
<div class="help-step-extra">
<ul>
<li><p class="Normal-indent">Click the <span class="Term-Soft">&lt;&lt; Collapse list</span> button if the <span class="Term-Soft">Custom 
 Paper Size...</span> button on the <span class="Term-Soft">Frequently Used 
 Settings</span> tab is not displayed.</p></li>
</ul>
</div>
<ol start="4">
<li><p>Enter the length and width of the paper as seen 
 in the graphic.</p></li>
</ol>
<div class="help-step-extra">
<ul>
<li><p class="Normal-indent">Enter the size 
 of the paper edge that is vertical relative to the feed direction of the 
 printer in <span class="Term-Soft">Width:</span>.</p></li>
<li><p class="Normal-indent">Enter the size 
 of the paper edge that is horizontal relative to the feed direction of 
 the printer in <span class="Term-Soft">Length:</span>.</p></li>
</ul>
</div>
<ol start="5">
<li><p>Click <span class="Term-Soft">OK</span> to close 
 the dialog box.</p></li>
<li><p>Place paper on a tray compatible with the custom 
 paper size.</p></li>
<li><p>Returning back to your computer, make any other 
 necessary settings, and then click <span class="Term-OS">OK</span>.<br/>
 The printing preferences dialog box closes.</p></li>
<li><p>Start printing.</p></li>
</ol>
<h2>Printing on Registered Custom Size Paper</h2>
<p class="Note">Preparation:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>Register the size of custom size paper that is 
 loaded in the printer properties dialog box in advance. For details, see 
 <a href="~/Topics/IDH_HOW_CUSTOMSIZEREG">Registering Custom Paper Sizes</a>.</p></li>
</ul>
<ol>
<li><p>Open the printing preferences dialog box after 
 creating a document in an application.</p></li>
<li><p>Click the <span class="Term-Soft">Frequently Used 
 Settings</span> tab or the <span class="Term-Soft">Basic</span> menu of 
 the <span class="Term-Soft">Detailed Settings</span> tab.</p></li>
<li><p>In the <span class="Term-Soft">Document Size:</span> 
 list, select the size of custom size paper you want to print on. The custom 
 paper sizes available in the list are those that have been registered 
 in advance.</p></li>
<li><p>Place paper on a tray compatible with the custom 
 paper size.</p></li>
<li><p>Returning back to your computer, make any other 
 necessary settings, and then click <span class="Term-OS">OK</span>.<br/>
 The printing preferences dialog box closes.</p></li>
<li><p>Start printing.</p></li>
</ol>
